Découvrez votre prochaine opportunité au sein d'une organisation qui compte parmi les 500 plus importantes entreprises mondiales. Envisagez des opportunités innovantes, découvrez notre culture enrichissante et travaillez avec des équipes talentueuses qui vous poussent à vous développer chaque jour. Nous savons ce qu’il faut faire pour diriger UPS vers l'avenir : des personnes passionnées dotées d’une combinaison unique de compétences. Si vous avez les qualités, de la motivation, de l'autonomie ou le leadership pour diriger des équipes, il existe des postes adaptés à vos aspirations et à vos compétences d'aujourd'hui et de demain.


**Fiche De Poste**
**RESPONSIBILITY:**
Tax responsibility for India express delivery, freight forwarding, contract logistics, airline, software and back-office businesses


**ROLE SUMMARY:**
Full time role for a Tax Supervisor located in Mumbai. The Tax Supervisor will be responsible for tax compliance, tax return preparation, tax advisory etc.


**How You’ll Spend Your Time**

* Handle (including prepare/review) all direct / indirect tax compliance process to ensure the timely filing of the Indian tax returns;
* Handle the tax audits, assessments, appeals in India, including attending hearings;
* Preparing all tax communications and correspondences to the tax offices or reviewing those prepared by the external adviser;
* Implement the UPS global transfer pricing strategy locally and work with US Corporate on transfer pricing documentation;
* Address any direct/indirect tax issues arising from operational / tax law changes and recommend solutions to the management;
* Liaise with the external tax advisors for practical advices on the tax implications of non-routine transactions, such as cross-border transactions, reorganizations, mergers and acquisitions etc., including negotiating with the local tax authorities and obtaining advance ruling, where applicable;
* Handle the tax accounting work, including the quarterly ASC 450 and 740 assessment for the uncertain tax positions and memo preparation;
* Attend to any tax related queries raised by the external auditors;
* Estimation and payment of local corporate tax and withholding taxes;
* To act as the contact point for the Indian tax related matters;
* Involve any other ad-hoc projects, including active participation in cross functional team discussions /projects concerning tax directly/ indirectly and contributing to the optimal tax outcome based on viable business solutions;
* Conduct health-checks and reviews on internal controls for the tax processes from time to time;
* Conduct trainings on tax topics for cross functional teams from time to time
* Independently handle GST audits and assessments

**Profile Requirements**

* Chartered Accountant with competencies in indirect taxes (especially GST), Indian corporate income and transfer pricing
* At least 2-5 years relevant working experience, preferably in a Big 4 CPA firm or niche consultancy firms in tax advisory, assessment and litigation
* Tax compliance and Tax return preparation skills
* Excellent analytical and problem solving skills
* Job specific competence: has accounting knowledge and has capability to research on any topic
* Should be a team player, self-motivated, result driven with ability to communicate clearly and concisely with personnel from different levels and both within and outside the organization
* Capable/proven decision maker, effectively bilingual (spoken and written)
* Strong command of the English Language, both written and verbal communication
* Good working knowledge in MS office

**Type De Contrat**
en CDI


*Chez UPS, égalité des chances, traitement équitable et environnement de travail inclusif sont des valeurs clefs auxquelles nous sommes attachés.*

The Service Manager, South India is responsible for leading and driving service operations, customer experience, and service business growth for the Medical Solutions business across South India. The incumbent will ensure operational excellence, profitable service delivery, strong customer satisfaction, effective distributor management, and the achievement of service revenue and business objectives while maintaining high standards of quality and compliance.










**Key Responsibilities** 



* Manage day\-to\-day service operations and ensure achievement of service KPIs and business objectives;
* Drive customer satisfaction through timely, high\-quality service support and issue resolution;
* Lead service revenue growth through service contracts, repairs, and other service offerings;
* Monitor and improve service processes, SOP compliance, and operational efficiency;
* Oversee service center performance, ensuring quality standards and turnaround time (TAT) targets are met;
* Manage service budgets, forecasts, costs, and profitability;
* Build and maintain strong relationships with customers, distributors, and key stakeholders;
* Monitor installed base (IB) coverage, service contract renewal rates, and service business performance;
* Ensure effective use of service systems and tools, including SFDC, for reporting and performance tracking;
* Conduct regular reviews of service quality and implement continuous improvement initiatives;
* Lead, coach, and develop the service team to achieve individual and team goals;
* Support regional service projects and new business initiatives as required;
* Ensure compliance with company policies, regulatory requirements, and quality standards.









**Qualifications:** 



* Bachelor's degree in Electronics Engineering, Medical Science, Technology, or a related field preferred.
* Minimum 5 years of experience in the medical device industry preferred.
* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with proficiency in the local language, Hindi, and/or English.
* Demonstrated ability to develop and execute effective sales strategies.
* Proficiency in CRM software and sales analytics tools.
* Ability to thrive in a fast\-paced, dynamic environment.









 If you believe you meet these qualifications, I encourage you to apply for the role.
